te trump  i continue to be stunned and appalled by  that reality i would love to talk to  some of those undecided voters i  invite you to call in i've not heard  from any of them so far  now it's really important to remember  that  a popular vote margin correlates  differently to the likelihood of an  electoral victory for democrats versus  republicans there is a  structural imbalance against democrats  where as you know  sometimes democrats win the popular vote  and don't become president because they  lose the electoral college as i'm sure  you remember  um unless you're four years old in which  case i don't even know that we have  four-year-olds in our audience  in 2016 donald trump lost the popular  vote by 2.1  but he won the electoral college thanks  to 70-something  thousand votes in three states nate  silver  from 538 did something important he  crunched the numbers to tell us  given a particular popular vote margin  how likely is it that joe biden will win  the electoral college  and again understand that the numbers  are skewed in this way  because of the urban rural divide and  because of some other  sort of base level factors that favor  republicans in the electoral college  uh even at the even while  being at a disadvantage in the popular  vote so  if joe biden wins the popular vote by  under one point his odds of becoming  president of  getting 270 electoral votes are only six  percent  if joe biden can win the popular vote by  one to two points  he has a 22 percent chance of winning  the electoral college  if joe biden matches hillary clinton's  popular vote win  somewhere in the two to three point  range it is still slightly more likely  that trump wins the electoral college in  other words if  biden gets a similar margin of victory  in the popular vote to hillary  he only has a 46 chance of winning the  electoral college  that's why we all have to vote only when  joe biden's popular vote lead gets  beyond three points  does joe biden become the like